    {
        "content": "<p>dhil opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14540\">PR #14540</a> from <code>dhil:stack-switching-bounds</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This patch adds a defensive check in <code>occupy_next_slot</code>, ensuring that a continuation's data buffer has sufficient capacity. I believe a well-typed Wasm program should never be able to fail this check, thus failing it ought to indicate some external tampering with continuation objects.</p>\n<p>Resolves #13028. Note the root cause in #13028 was fixed by PR#11717. This PR resolves the issue in the sense that it adds the defensive suggestion outlined in the issue.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 629275252,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791212784
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>dhil requested <a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14540\">PR #14540</a>.</p>",
